# Competency question: "What are the statistics conformance-failure classes, each shown by an
# ill-formed exemplar?" Exercises the failure vocabulary of the STATISTICS charter: each way a
# statistical object can be ill-formed is a first-class subclass of math:MathConformanceFailure
# that the slice's SHACL shapes raise. The fixture instantiates one exemplar of each failure,
# and the reasoning-free query reads back each exemplar's asserted failure type. Scoped so the
# exemplar is fixture-local and the type is math:. Over the fixture the answer is exactly the
# nine statistics failure classes {math:UnderspecifiedEstimate, math:ImplicitMissingness,
# math:IllFramedPValue, math:IntervalKindConflation, math:IncompleteConfidenceInterval,
# math:IncompleteCredibleInterval, math:UnframedEffectSize, math:UnanchoredDiagnostic,
# math:CalibrationSenseConflation}.
PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>

SELECT ?exemplar ?failure WHERE {
    ?exemplar a ?failure .
    FILTER(STRSTARTS(STR(?exemplar), "http://example.org/math/"))
    FILTER(STRSTARTS(STR(?failure), "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/"))
}
ORDER BY ?exemplar
